# Blog Framework Diagrams

Framework diagrams live in `assets/img/blog/{media}-{YYYY-MM-DD}/{slug}-framework.mmd` + `.svg`, matching the post's `media_type` (or `site` for main blog) and date. Embed at the top of both `content_zh` and `content_en` in bilingual posts.

Substack covers: see `.cursor/rules/substack-cover-art.mdc` → `assets/img/blog/{media}-{YYYY-MM-DD}/cover.png`

## Structure (follow existing good diagrams)

Use **`flowchart TB` only** — no `flowchart LR`, no `subgraph`.

Layout is **top-down with horizontal branch tiers**, like `make-profitable-framework.mmd` and `ai-asymmetric-advantage-framework.mmd`. Never a single-node-per-row chain for 3+ steps (pure vertical), and never a single horizontal chain (pure LR).

```
core (1–2 nodes, dark blue stadium)
  ==> 2–3 sibling mains (light blue, same tier — spreads horizontally)
    optional one sub-detail level (gray) under each main
      ==> goal (1 node, green stadium)
```

Each parent that branches must fan out to **2–3 siblings** at the next tier before converging again.

## Node classes (always define all four)

```mermaid
classDef core fill:#2c5282,color:#fff,stroke:#1a365d,stroke-width:3px
classDef main fill:#ebf4ff,color:#1a365d,stroke:#4299e1,stroke-width:2px
classDef sub fill:#edf2f7,color:#4a5568,stroke:#cbd5e0
classDef goal fill:#276749,color:#fff,stroke:#22543d,stroke-width:2px
```

- **core** `(["..."])` — central thesis (1–2 nodes max)
- **main** `["..."]` — key branches (2–3 max)
- **sub** `["..."]` — one extra detail level only; short phrases, not lists
- **goal** `(["..."])` — single conclusion / action

## Arrows

- `==>` primary flow (core → main → goal)
- `-->` secondary / detail links
- `-.->` optional tension or mismatch (sparingly)

## Content rules

- **Refined, not exhaustive** — reader grasps the idea at a glance (~4–8 nodes total)
- **Clear hierarchy** — not a flat chain of same-weight boxes
- **English only** in diagram text and caption (bilingual posts keep diagram in English)
- Caption below image: one-line `Core idea: …`

## Regenerate SVG after editing `.mmd`

```bash
npx @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli -i assets/img/blog/{media}-{YYYY-MM-DD}/{slug}-framework.mmd -o assets/img/blog/{media}-{YYYY-MM-DD}/{slug}-framework.svg -b transparent
```

## Reference examples

- Two cores + branches: `site-2026-01-25/make-profitable-framework.mmd`
- One core + parallel mains: `site-2025-08-22/systematic-thinking-framework.mmd`, `site-2025-12-08/ai-agents-framework.mmd`
- Core chain + tier + goal: `site-2026-06-25/ai-asymmetric-advantage-framework.mmd`
